## 🎭 4.2 Page Object Generation (NEW COMPONENTS ONLY)

Reference: **[Layered Architecture](mdc:ArchitectureLayeredDesign.mdc)**

### **Generate Page Objects for NEW Components**

**Source Information**:
- Use **[Phase 0](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)** `ReusabilityAnalysis.md` to identify which Page Objects to CREATE
- Use **[Phase 1](mdc:Phase1_LocatorResearch.mdc)** `ElementsCollected.ts` for element definitions
- Use `locator_cache.json` for locator references

**DO NOT Generate**:
- SKIP Page Objects marked as "EXISTING" in `ReusabilityAnalysis.md`
- Reuse existing Page Objects without modification (unless extension planned in Phase 0)

**Requirements**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Extend `Engine/Shared/AIPage.ts` base class
- **(MANDATORY)** Use AIElement for ALL element interactions
- **(MANDATORY)** NO direct `this.page.locator()`, `this.page.click()`, `this.page.fill()` calls
- **(MANDATORY)** Initialize AIElement instances with cache keys matching `locator_cache.json`
- **(MANDATORY)** Wrap all methods with `TestLogger.pageStep()`
- **(MANDATORY)** Use human-readable descriptions (NO locators/selectors in method names)

**Table View Pages**:
- If page has table view matching reference examples, extend `AITomsPage` instead of `AIPage`
- Use default or custom table configuration
- Store table configuration in `locator_cache.json`

**Example Pattern**:
```typescript
import { Page } from '@playwright/test';
import { AIElement } from 'Engine/Shared/AIElement';
import { AIPage } from 'Engine/Shared/AIPage';
import { TestLogger } from 'Engine/Shared/TestLogger';

export class DashboardPage extends AIPage {
    private menuButton: AIElement;
    private profileLink: AIElement;
    private logoutButton: AIElement;

    constructor(page: Page) {
        super(page, 'DashboardPage');
        
        // Use extended natural language descriptions to clearly identify elements
        this.menuButton = new AIElement(this, 'menuButton', 'Main navigation menu button in the top left corner');
        this.profileLink = new AIElement(this, 'profileLink', 'User profile link in the top right navigation bar');
        this.logoutButton = new AIElement(this, 'logoutButton', 'Logout button in the user dropdown menu');
    }

    async navigateToDashboard(baseUrl: string): Promise<void> {
        await TestLogger.pageStep('Navigate to dashboard', async () => {
            await this.navigateTo(`${baseUrl}/#dashboard`);
            await this.waitForPageLoad();
            TestLogger.info('Dashboard loaded');
        });
    }

    async clickMenu(): Promise<void> {
        await TestLogger.pageStep('Click menu button', async () => {
            await this.menuButton.waitFor({ timeout: 3000 });
            await this.menuButton.click();
            TestLogger.info('Menu opened');
        });
    }
}

export default DashboardPage;
```

